{"corpus": "o222-no-go-boundary-charter-v1 / o224-r1-contract-v1", "definitions": [["a", "phase layer", "Can a non-trivial complex-phase (U(1)) factor group be generated from K_chain (x) K_tree WITHOUT leaving the frozen inventory?", "DECISION: (i) compute the commutator subgroup [2I,2I]  --  if it equals 2I then Hom(2I,U(1)) is trivial and no non-trivial phase CHARACTER exists; (ii) test whether every element is conjugate to its inverse  --  iff true, every irreducible character is real-valued, so no genuinely complex (Frobenius-Schur indicator 0) irrep exists; (iii) compute the Frobenius-Schur indicator of the faithful 2-dim (spin) representation nu = (1/120) sum_g chi(g^2) with chi(g) = 2 Re(w_g)  --  nu = -1 means quaternionic (a complex structure J EXISTS but is symplectic, not U(1)); (iv) count order-4 elements and check g^2 = -1.  VERDICT: RED (impossibility inside the frozen inventory) iff (i)-(iv) all hold as stated; GREEN would require an explicit zero-parameter complex-phase construction passing the four hard tests."], ["a2", "phase layer / minimal cost", "What is the minimal-cost geometry of a phase extension?", "DECISION: the carrier of a genuinely complex irrep must contain an element not conjugate to its inverse; enumerate the smallest group orders that admit such elements (a theorem-level statement, not a search over IDCM numbers) AND locate the phase sector that already exists in IDCM (W-field Goldstone phase) by CITATION of the owning O (no re-derivation). VERDICT: RED for the frozen protocol, with the escape route named."], ["b", "bipartite tensor layer", "Can the bipartiteness of K_tree be the source of a tensor factorisation H_A (x) H_B, and is the single-system kernel (2I subset SU(2)) accidental or structurally necessary?", "DECISION: (i) compute the full commutator census of the 62 readout observables diag(K[.][a])  --  all abelian => maximally classical; (ii) count the distinct readout rows (the readout algebra dimension); (iii) exhaustive audit of every bipartition candidate induced by the axis TYPES (3^4 x classes) of the CHSH tuple: max|S| per class; VERDICT: RED iff all classes stay <= 2 and the readout algebra is abelian, GREEN iff an explicit bipartite factorisation with non-commuting factors exists."], ["c", "B6 multiparty", "Do GHZ / Mermin / Klyshko type multiparty non-classical correlations exist in the frozen machine?", "DECISION: (i) PROOF: the frozen protocol assigns ONE setting-independent world state per pass (R_indep = 1) and every readout is a deterministic function of (state, own setting) only => the joint law is a mixture of product laws with lambda = the world state => it is a local hidden variable model => every Mermin-Klyshko inequality holds at its classical bound (n=3 : 2, n=4 : 2); (ii) EXHAUSTIVE enumeration of the n=3 Mermin expression over all 62^3 tuples (zero pruning, exact) and of the n=4 Mermin-Klyshko expression over all 62^4 tuples (zero pruning, exact); (iii) CALIBRATION: the same enumerator applied to a genuine 3-qubit GHZ model must return 4 (= 2^{(n+1)/2}) and to the 2-qubit singlet 2*sqrt2, proving the enumerator has discriminating power.  VERDICT: RED iff (i) holds on all three levels and the enumerations confirm the bounds; GREEN iff some tuple exceeds the classical bound."], ["d", "value-set necessity", "Is the discrete value set {0, 1/15, 2/15, 1/5, 4/15, 1/3, 2/3, 1} a representation-theoretic necessity of 2I (i.e. can a continuous-angle structure give it)?", "DECISION: (i) exact value set of C1 and C2 over all 3844 pairs (and 120-denominator numerator divisibility); (ii) structural decomposition: K[s][a] = K[-s][a] (centre Z2) => C1 = 2 * (sum over A5)/120 => values are k/15 IFF the A5-sum is divisible by 4; test exhaustively; (iii) candidate mechanisms: left-invariance of K under subgroups (order 2/4/8/10), the antipodal vertex count, and a RANDOM-GENERIC-AXIS control (>=300 draws) testing whether the divisibility is axis-specific or group-forced; (iv) the CONTINUOUS control: replace the +-1 binarisation by the exact inner product value (the un-binarised readout) and recompute the correlator value set.  VERDICT: RED iff the quantisation is forced by the +-1 sign readout on the discrete 2I orbit (surviving the generic-axis control), with the continuum unreachable inside the frozen protocol."], ["e", "F1/F2 operationalisation", "Operationalise the F1/F2 criteria (docs/39) into a mechanical decision procedure and test whether an achievable-depth > 1 construct can appear in the frozen architecture.", "DECISION: F1 = a decision procedure taking (state space, readout set, state) and returning (a) complex-phase-dof present?, (b) bipartite tensor factorisation present? ; it must PASS a calibration set {2-qubit singlet: must pass both, 3-qubit GHZ: pass both, frozen machine: fail both, product state: fail both, commuting pair: fail both}.  F2 = a verifier taking a claimed max|S| and deciding whether the construct lies inside the frozen domain (all ingredients must be functions of the frozen primitives).  DEPTH: operational definition = maximum number of conditionally independent lambda fragments; theorem = determinism gives depth 1; mechanically re-derive the 120 -> 60 behaviour collapse (class size 2).  VERDICT: GREEN iff F1 separates the calibration set and depth > 1 is exhibited; RED iff F1 has discriminating power AND the frozen machine fails both clauses and depth > 1 is impossible."]], "frozen_sha256": {"04_b2_settings.json": "2357006c68e0165dc9fd7d8d73524593a776e1bf6a8b62ddbc8dc2c1a8af20ee", "08_a2_h_table.json": "adeaf8a7fb5495ea57be194c1a704c973a9208026cdd10ef615cd59c58005b66", "09_a2_correlation.json": "dbe664760d3648bd5591f5c43a6ab5ef69bcf9c5834893bc0d907df5e561942e"}, "operational_space": {"S0_state_space": "state space = G = 2I (order 120) in its LEFT REGULAR action (120 states), uniform measure 1/120; the canonical element order of O222 scripts/09 is used verbatim", "S1_readout": "readout = +-1 REAL SIGN of the 62 frozen icosian directions (30 edge + 20 face + 12 vertex), K[i][a] = sgn(u_a . R_{g_i} n_0), tie rule H3 = sign of the first non-zero component of R_{g_i} n_0", "S2_correlation": "pair-local factor table + memo (E1 fresh-state control / E2 persistent ledger, frozen order); window all4 = four settings pairwise distinct and no antipodal pair; budget = 44 reads = N_d = 1 tick", "S3_zero_param": "zero new parameters; no post-hoc operator fitting; no phi-power fitting; every judged quantity must be a function of frozen inputs only", "S4_exact": "all judging arithmetic exact (Fraction / Q(sqrt5)); floats allowed for display only", "S5_write_scope": "no writes outside open_problems_fresh/o224_amplitude_complex_phase_layer/"}, "predictions": [["P1", "relock: |2I| = 120, K = 120x62 with +1/-1 = 3720/3720, all 62 column sums = 0", "reproduced", "frozen"], ["P2", "relock: our C1 (numerator/120) equals data/frozen/09_a2_correlation.json C1_num on all 3844 entries, 0 mismatches", "reproduced", "frozen"], ["P3", "relock: max|S| = 2 for E1 all4 and = 3 for E2 all4; 4 for the distinct statistic (both E1 and E2)", "reproduced", "frozen"], ["P4", "relock: value set of C1 = {0, +-1/15, +-2/15, +-1/5, +-4/15, +-1/3, +-2/3, +-1} (the docs/45 B2 set, reproduced)", "reproduced", "frozen"], ["P5", "a: [2I,2I] = 2I (2I perfect) => Hom(2I,U(1)) trivial; exactly ONE 1-dim irrep", "predicted", "blind"], ["P6", "a: every g conjugate to g^-1 => all irreducible characters of 2I are real-valued => NO genuinely complex irrep; Frobenius-Schur indicator of the faithful 2-dim rep = -1 (quaternionic); exactly 30 elements of order 4 and g^2 = -1 for each", "predicted", "blind"], ["P7", "b: the 62 readout observables are simultaneously diagonal => 0 of 226920 commutators non-zero; the number of DISTINCT readout rows is small (<= 62) and the readout algebra is abelian", "predicted", "blind"], ["P8", "b: the maximal |S| over every axis-type class of the quadruple stays <= 2 (no bipartition-by-type raises the bound)", "predicted", "blind"], ["P9", "c: max |Mermin_3| over all 62^3 tuples <= 2 EXACT (classical bound), and the same for Mermin-Klyshko n=4 over all 62^4 tuples", "predicted", "blind"], ["P10", "c calibration: the same enumerator returns 4 for the 3-qubit GHZ Mermin expression and 2*sqrt2 for the 2-qubit singlet CHSH expression (discriminating power)", "predicted", "blind"], ["P11", "c: the explicit LHV certificate (lambda = world state, 120 values, uniform) reconstructs the enumerated 3-party correlations exactly", "predicted", "blind"], ["P12", "d: ALL 3844 C1 numerators are divisible by 8 (values are multiples of 1/15 in 120ths)", "reproduced (seen pre-contract by an exploratory probe -- disclosed)", "partially seen"], ["P13", "d: the quantisation survives a >=300-draw random-generic-axis control, i.e. it is forced by the +-1 sign readout on the discrete 2I orbit, not by the particular 62 axis directions", "partially seen (300 draws seen pre-contract -- disclosed)"], ["P14", "d: replacing the +-1 binarisation by the exact inner-product readout widens the value set (the continuum is destroyed by the sign map, not by the group)", "predicted (structure seen qualitatively pre-contract: the 12-fibre readout quotient and the Z2 collapse were observed by probe)", "partially seen"], ["P15", "e: F1 separates the 5-element calibration set exactly; the frozen machine fails both F1 clauses; depth > 1 is impossible (behaviour collapse 120 -> 60, class size 2)", "predicted", "blind"], ["P16", "four hard tests: (1) zero-parameter cost counted explicitly; (2) Monte-Carlo null for the numeric claims; (3) out-of-sample blind prediction = P9/P13/P14 values, written before the corresponding runs; (4) structural rigidity = perturbation battery (random axis draws, h-table scramble, state relabelling) leaves every RED verdict standing", "predicted", "blind"]], "seen_disclosure": ["An exploratory probe (scratch, not part of the deliverable) was run BEFORE this contract was written.  It revealed: (i) the 120 state rows of K take exactly 12 distinct values with all fibres of size 10; (ii) the value set of C1 is the docs/45 B2 8-magnitude set; (iii) all C1 numerators are divisible by 8; (iv) K[s][a] = K[-s][a] for all s,a; (v) a 300-draw random-axis control returned A5-sum divisible by 4 in every draw.", "Consequently P4, P12 and P13 are NOT blind: they are disclosed here as re-verifications rather than blind predictions.  Every other prediction is blind at the time of writing.  No verdict of this round depends on the probe alone: each is recomputed exhaustively and independently in scripts/01-07."], "self_sha256": "16f1b0a14b6fbd75a1ff4f700bb192ce7b13a218832e312c9e67989233be453c", "verdict_rule": {"FORBIDDEN": "\"unclear\" / \"not yet determined\" is not an admissible verdict for (a)-(e)", "GREEN": "explicit zero-parameter construction, all four hard tests passed", "RED": "explicit impossibility proof inside the frozen inventory"}}
